# {{ project-name }}

Runnable Axum reference service generated from the Rust Web Foundry Project Template.

The generated service includes a canonical Task create-and-lookup vertical slice. It demonstrates Clean Architecture boundaries, explicit boundary conversions, private database and wire models, checked SQLx persistence, outbound Ports, HTTP contracts, observability, and process lifecycle. Task is a reference slice, not a universal task-management domain model.

## Prerequisites

- Rustup
- Docker with Compose v2
- curl
- cargo-generate `>=0.23.14, <0.24.0`
- Just `>=1.58.0, <2.0.0`
- sqlx-cli `>=0.9.0, <0.10.0`

```sh
rustup update stable
cargo install cargo-generate --version 0.23.14 --locked
cargo install just --version 1.58.0 --locked
cargo install sqlx-cli --version 0.9.0 --locked --no-default-features --features rustls,mysql
```

## Verify the generated service

```sh
just verify
```

For direct operation, copy `.env.example` to `.env`, then run migrations and the server separately:

```sh
cargo run -p {{ project-name }} -- migrate
cargo run -p {{ project-name }} -- serve
```

The server never runs migrations. Configuration and lifecycle details are in [the Guide](docs/guide/README.md).

## Architecture

```text
http ────────────┐
                 ├──> application ───> domain
infrastructure ──┘

app ──> http + infrastructure + application + domain
```

Source, tests, manifests, migrations, and quality commands are the executable specification. Start changes from the nearest complete production path; use the Guide only for a concrete unanswered design question. See [architecture](docs/guide/architecture/README.md), the [selected stack](docs/guide/stack.md), the [Task flow](docs/guide/task-flow.md), and [development](docs/guide/development.md).

## Rust review

The project pins `leonardomso/rust-skills` for fresh, review-only use and applies project-specific overrides for Clean Architecture and the selected stack:

```sh
bash scripts/install-rust-skills.sh
```

Then explicitly invoke `.agents/skills/review-rust-web/SKILL.md` in a fresh review session with the request and complete diff. See [Reviewing changes](docs/guide/reviewing.md).

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `just infra-up` / `just infra-down` | Start or stop local MySQL |
| `just policy-stub` | Run the local TaskPolicy example |
| `just migrate` | Apply embedded migrations explicitly |
| `just sqlx-prepare` | Apply development migrations and refresh `.sqlx` query metadata |
| `just serve` | Start the production server path |
| `just test` | Run every workspace test against an existing MySQL |
| `just architecture` | Check workspace dependencies and the small project/review contract |
| `just check` | Run architecture checks, format, Clippy, and DB-free tests |
| `just ci` | Run checks, MySQL integration, query verification, and live smoke against an existing MySQL |
| `just verify` | Start MySQL and prove the fresh service end to end |
